  "title": "Debug Faulty Priority Encoder Wiring",
  "description": "A 4-to-2 Priority Encoder (I3 > I2 > I1 > I0) is pre-wired on the breadboard using 7404 (NOT) and 7432 (OR) ICs. However, due to a wrong wire routing from SW2 (I2), selecting input I2 incorrectly lights up LED0 instead of LED1. Inspect the pre-wired circuit and re-route the faulty wire so SW2 properly produces Y1=1, Y0=0.",
